  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The Perfekt",
   "texto": [
    "To tell what you did, the **Perfekt** is used: the present of **haben** + the **participio**, which goes **al final** of the phrase. **Ich habe einen Film gesehen** (I saw a film; literally «I've seen a movie.»).",
    "When speaking, it serves both «vi» and «I've seen»."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "How the participle is formed",
   "texto": [
    "The regular verbs: **ge-** + root + **-t**. machen → **gemacht**, kaufen → **gekauft**, spielen → **gespielt**. If the root ends in -t: arbeiten → **gearbeitet**.",
    "The irregular end up in **-en** and sometimes change the vocal: essen → **gegessen**, sehen → **gesehen**, lesen → **gelesen**, trinken → **getrunken**.",
    "The verbs that start with **be-** or **ver-** do not carry «ge-»: besuchen → **besucht**."
   ]
  },
